e social board a dozen times within her memory; and while Judy Trenor was obdurate there was small chance of…”"},{"id":"mrs-trenor","name":"Mrs. Trenor","role":"minor","group":"g-trenor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: ““Mrs.”"},{"id":"mrs-dorset","name":"Mrs. Dorset","role":"minor","group":"g-dorset","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “Mrs.”"},{"id":"mrs-hatch","name":"Mrs. Hatch","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s24","summary":"First mention: “Fisher had not specified the line her friend was to take; she owned herself unacquainted with Mrs.”"},{"id":"duchess","name":"Duchess","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: “Besides, Lady Cressida is the Duchess of Beltshire’s sister, and I naturally supposed she was the same sort; but you never can tell in those English families.”"},{"id":"jack-stepney","name":"Jack Stepney","aliases":["Jack","Mrs. Jack Stepney"],"role":"minor","group":"g-stepney","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “On his first appearance—when her improvident cousin, Jack Stepney, had obtained for him (in return for favours too easily guessed) a card to one of the vast impersonal Van Osburgh “crushes”—Rosedale, with that mixture…”"},{"id":"van-osburgh","name":"Van Osburgh","aliases":["Miss Van Osburgh","Mrs. Van Osburgh"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “It isn’t a bit hotter here than in Mrs.”"},{"id":"bertha-dorset","name":"Bertha Dorset","role":"minor","group":"g-dorset","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “But of course she had lost—she who needed every penny, while Bertha Dorset, whose husband showered money on her, must have pocketed at least five hundred, and Judy Trenor, who could have afforded to lose a thousand a…”"},{"id":"mrs-bry","name":"Mrs. Bry","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s10","summary":"First mention: “Mrs.”"},{"id":"mattie-gormer","name":"Mattie Gormer","aliases":["Mrs. Gormer","Mattie"],"role":"minor","firstAppearanc